# PHASE 12 — POINT 8: pin line endings for checksum-bearing files.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prisma records `_prisma_migrations.checksum` as a hash over the RAW BYTES of
# the `migration.sql` it applied. Without a `.gitattributes`, a checkout on a
# machine with `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Windows, and the setting on
# at least one machine that works on this repository) materialises those files
# with CRLF, while CI's Linux checkout materialises them with LF. The commit is
# identical; the bytes are not.
#
# The consequence is not cosmetic. A database migrated from the LF artifact and
# then deployed from the CRLF one fails with "migration ... was modified after
# it was applied", and `prisma migrate deploy` stops — mid-release, on the
# migration it refuses to re-apply. It was measured, not theorised: `git
# archive` on this repository injected 21 CR bytes into
# `20270924000000_drop_workspace_persona_profiles`, whose canonical blob has
# none.
#
# So every file whose bytes are hashed, signed, or compared is pinned to LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Migration SQL — hashed into `_prisma_migrations.checksum`.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Fixture and evidence artifacts that are digested or byte-compared.
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.pem text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail to execute on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
